cff-version: 1.2.0
message: |
  Citation metadata for the spektrafilm 0.3.4 runtime packaged in this
  repository, including local CPU and memory changes. Andrea Volpato is the
  upstream author. This is not an official spektrafilm release and it has no
  Zenodo DOI.

  Upstream CITATION.cff on main still says version 0.3.2, doi "xxxxx", and
  license GPL-3.0-or-later. Those values are not repeated here. "xxxxx" is a
  placeholder, not a DOI. The license identifier below follows the upstream
  pyproject.toml field "GPLv3", the upstream README statement "GPLv3 licensed",
  and GPL-3 section 14: the program texts that were compared do not say
  "or any later version".

  If you find spektrafilm useful, acknowledge it and cite
  https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm once that project publishes a
  real DOI.

authors:
  - family-names: "Volpato"
    given-names: "Andrea"
    email: "volpedellenevi@gmail.com"
    orcid: "0000-0003-3368-0017"
    affiliation: "KTH Royal Institute of Technology, Sweden"

title: "spektrafilm: spectral simulation of analog photography"
version: "0.3.4"
repository-code: "https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm"
license: "GPL-3.0-only"
url: "https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm"
